<title>SWEDEN: Autoliv sees price pressure continuing.</title>
<headline>Autoliv sees price pressure continuing.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish/U.S. car safety equipment group Autoliv Inc. said on Monday it expected significant price pressure in the U.S. to continue for another six months to a year while pressure in Europe would continue but not so severely.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect the price pressure (in the U.S.) to continue for half a year to one year,&quot; Autoliv chief executive and chairman Gunnar Bark told a telephone conference.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't see (a fall of) two digit figures in Europe but it will be there in the U.S. for this year and early 1998.&quot;</p>
</text>
